From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: jz4740: accept the T20 SDIO voltage window

The Wyze Cam 2 T20 SDIO WiFi is powered from a 3.0 V rail and
advertises only MMC_VDD_29_30/30_31. The host currently offers
3.2-3.4 V, so CMD5 succeeds but mmc_select_voltage() rejects the
card with 'no support for card's volts'.

Accept the 3.0 V window as well.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c
@@ -1146,7 +1146,9 @@
 		mmc->f_max = JZ_MMC_CLK_RATE;
 
 	mmc->f_min = mmc->f_max / 128;
-	mmc->ocr_avail = MMC_VDD_32_33 | MMC_VDD_33_34;
+	/* T20 SDIO WiFi cards advertise the 3.0 V window. */
+	mmc->ocr_avail = MMC_VDD_29_30 | MMC_VDD_30_31 |
+			 MMC_VDD_32_33 | MMC_VDD_33_34;
 
 	/*
 	 * We use a fixed timeout of 5s, hence inform the core about it. A
